1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:03,363
Every neural network begins with one simple

2
00:00:03,523 --> 00:00:03,783
unit:

3
00:00:04,344 --> 00:00:05,546
an artificial neuron.

4
00:00:06,307 --> 00:00:07,328
It takes numbers in,

5
00:00:07,849 --> 00:00:09,350
multiplies each by a weight,

6
00:00:09,831 --> 00:00:10,552
adds them together,

7
00:00:11,013 --> 00:00:13,295
and passes the total through an activation

8
00:00:13,355 --> 00:00:15,839
curve—deciding how strongly to fire.

9
00:00:16,769 --> 00:00:19,532
Wire thousands of these neurons into stacked

10
00:00:19,592 --> 00:00:20,032
layers,

11
00:00:20,293 --> 00:00:21,554
and a pattern emerges.

12
00:00:22,295 --> 00:00:25,018
Signals ripple forward from layer to layer.

13
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:26,760
When the answer is wrong,

14
00:00:27,201 --> 00:00:30,504
an error signal flows backward—and training gently

15
00:00:30,605 --> 00:00:33,248
nudges every weight until the network learns.

16
00:00:34,278 --> 00:00:34,439
Now,

17
00:00:34,699 --> 00:00:36,601
how does a network read language?

18
00:00:37,463 --> 00:00:37,763
First,

19
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:41,188
it slices text into bite-sized pieces called

20
00:00:41,268 --> 00:00:41,688
tokens.

21
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:45,173
Each token maps to a vector—a list

22
00:00:45,213 --> 00:00:47,336
of numbers placing that word in a

23
00:00:47,476 --> 00:00:48,418
map of meaning.

24
00:00:49,348 --> 00:00:51,651
A large language model reads your prompt

25
00:00:51,932 --> 00:00:53,314
and asks one question:

26
00:00:53,934 --> 00:00:54,836
what comes next?

27
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,100
It scores every token in its vocabulary,

28
00:00:58,521 --> 00:00:59,482
picks a likely winner,

29
00:01:00,003 --> 00:01:01,004
tacks it onto the end,

30
00:01:01,465 --> 00:01:03,868
and repeats—one word at a time.

31
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:08,042
What makes a transformer smart is self-attention.

32
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:11,445
In 'The animal didn't cross the street

33
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:14,489
because it was too tired,' attention lets

34
00:01:14,509 --> 00:01:17,432
'it' look across the sentence and lock

35
00:01:17,572 --> 00:01:20,675
onto 'animal.' Stack dozens of these layers,

36
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:22,678
and deep context clicks.

37
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,531
Put it all together on one board:

38
00:01:26,192 --> 00:01:27,434
words become tokens,

39
00:01:27,954 --> 00:01:29,276
tokens become vectors,

40
00:01:30,037 --> 00:01:33,081
attention weighs the context across stacked layers,

41
00:01:33,702 --> 00:01:36,847
and out comes the next token—prediction by

42
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:37,428
prediction.
